so I was just reading section 8.5 of the CLL and read this: "Relative
clauses introduced by ``voi'' are restrictive, like those introduced
by ``poi''. However, there is a fundamental difference between ``poi''
and ``voi'' relative clauses. A ``poi'' relative clause is said to be
veridical, in the same sense that a description using ``lo'' or
``loi'' is: it is essential to the interpretation that the bridi
actually be true".

Now, given xorlo, how does poi/voi work?

